# DEM (Yade) tutorial cases for the Yade regression runner (Allrun.yade).
# Requires: solver built with ./build.sh --yade, Yade installed, mpirun available.
#
# Format: one case path per line (relative to repo root).
# The case's Allrun must exit 0 on success and assert its own output
# (sphere/spring VTK existence checks are already in each case's Allrun).
#
# Run with:
#   applications/test/regression/Allrun.yade

tutorials/cases/MicroTGA-DEM_Us_UsInterp

# lambdaMode exactDifferential fixtures: each starts the packed bed hot
# (Ts=800 K solid, T=850 K gas, so both heat transfer and pyrolysis chemistry
# are active within the fixture's short 2 ms run) and asserts the sign of
# lambdaDot over solid cells (porosityF < criticalPorosity) via
# applications/test/regression/tools/checkFieldSign.py, invoked from each
# case's own Allrun. ...Off is the "off" reduction: exactDifferential with
# every coefficient at its 0.0 default, which must give lambdaDot = 0 exactly.
#
# These four also exercise the reverse (YADE -> PGF) lambda channel, since
# YADE integrates State::lambda_ from the lambdaDot they produce and PGF
# interpolates it back into the lambda field. That path needs Foam-Yade and PGF
# built from matching revisions -- the particle-data buffer stride is a
# compile-time constant on both sides, with no MPI-level negotiation.
#
# The signs asserted by ...Chemistry and ...Both are honest statements about
# these fixtures' own dlambdaOverDYmi (2.5e-6, tuned so both terms stay
# visible at fixture scale -- see each dict's own comment), not a physics
# claim. A physically calibrated dlambdaOverDYmi is nearer 1e-3 m^4/kg (see
# README's lambdaDict reference), which would swamp the temperature term at
# this scale and flip ...Both's asserted positive sign.
tutorials/cases/MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotOff
tutorials/cases/MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotTemperature
tutorials/cases/MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotChemistry
tutorials/cases/MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotBoth

# Same chemistry-driven-only setup as ...Chemistry (dlambdaOverDTs 0, negative
# lambdaDot sign asserted the same way), but exercising three lambdaDict
# configuration paths the four fixtures above never touch: a non-default
# lambdaInterpolationMode (laplaceAnchored instead of the laplaceSetValues
# default), a per-specie dlambdaOverDYmi subdict instead of one uniform
# scalar, and a non-default lambdaBackgroundValue. See the case's own
# constant/lambdaDict for what each key does and why the two species it
# gives a nonzero coefficient to (wood, char1) were picked over the other two
# (char, hum). A fourth untested path, interpolateLambda false, is
# deliberately not a committed fixture -- it is a diagnostic-only fallback
# nobody is expected to select; it was instead exercised once as a throwaway
# /scratch run, recorded in lambdaDot-yade-owned-lambda-followup-2026-09-02.md
# Block B rather than checked in here.
tutorials/cases/MicroTGA-DEM_lambdaDotAltInterp

# tutorials/cases/simple_line_case is NOT listed yet. It builds, meshes and
# reaches the coupled loop, but its Allrun does not exit 0 under
# tools/runDEMCase.sh: the run aborts on the heap corruption that also trips
# the serial tier at teardown, and under --short Yade stops at the step cap
# while the solver is still waiting for the next coupling exchange, so
# "RUN FINISH" is never printed. List it once it exits 0.
